course: dictionary
lesson: 10247
title: Reading the clues: tomb
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A tomb is a grave, often a stone room where a dead body is laid, sometimes with a big stone or monument over it. You can work out this meaning from the words around it. «Tutankhamun's tomb was found almost untouched in 1922» tells you a tomb is a place where a body is kept, and the year tells you it was found by people digging.
explain: Some words do not give the whole story alone. «At the tomb of his friend Lazarus, Jesus wept, and then he called Lazarus back to life.» The clues are friend, wept and back to life: a tomb holds a dead person, and a grave is the place where it happens. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: A tomb can also be a cave cut in rock. At Easter, pupils hear how the women found «the empty tomb» on Easter morning. Christians believe Jesus rose from the dead, so the tomb was empty. The clue is the word empty: a tomb is not always full.
fact: A tomb is a grave, or a stone room where a dead body is laid.
fact: A tomb is often marked by a big stone or monument.
fact: In the Bible, the tomb of Jesus was a cave cut in rock.
fact: Phrases: «an ancient tomb» means a very old tomb, and «silent as the tomb» means very, very quiet.
fact: Pharaohs' tombs were often filled with treasure, and archaeologists dig them up to learn about the past.
exercise: In «Tutankhamun's tomb was found almost untouched in 1922», what is a tomb? | A tall tower built for a king | *A grave or stone room where a dead body is laid | A boat for crossing rivers | A cave where animals sleep
exercise: «At the tomb of his friend Lazarus, Jesus wept.» What was the tomb of Lazarus? | A market where people trade | A tall church bell tower | *A grave where a dead man was laid | A palace with gardens
exercise: «The library was silent as the tomb.» What does this phrase mean? | Full of noise and laughter | *Very, very quiet | Very old | Dark and cold
test: Which word means nearly the same as tomb? | *grave | river | castle | cave
test: On Easter morning, what did the women find at the tomb? | A new king sleeping inside | A crowd of soldiers guarding it | A golden mask | *The tomb empty, because Jesus had risen
exam: What do archaeologists do with ancient tombs? | They use them as homes for families | They paint the walls white | They fill them with sand to hide them | *They dig them up to learn about the past
